-- text.w40 --
rex — Runtime Executive for Agents  dev

Usage:
  rex
    open the board (TUI)
  rex --quiet-boot
    open the board without boot sounds
  rex <command> [flags]

Sessions:
  ls [flags]
    list sessions
  new [flags] -- <prompt>
    start a session (-tool -model -cwd)
  attach <sel> [flags]
    open a session (ctrl+] detaches)
  here
    open the board for this workspace
    (needs workspaces)
  reply <sel> [flags] -- <text>
    answer a session that needs input
  send <sel> [flags] -- <text>
    send raw input (stdin when no text)
  wait <sel> [flags]
    block until a session reaches a
    state
  rename <sel> <slug>
    change a session's slug
  name <sel> [-clear] [-- <text>]
    set, show or clear the display name
  done <sel> [-after 72h]
    mark done; cleared after
    retire_after_hours
  undone <sel>
    cancel a pending done
  archive <sel>
    archive a session
  resume <sel> [-print]
    respawn an exited session (-print:
    only the resume id)
  undo <sel> [-turns N] [-yes]
    restore the folder to before the
    last turn
  redo <sel> [-yes]
    bring back what undo replaced
  complete <sel>
    stop a session now and mark it done
  rm <sel> [-force]
    delete a session (-force without a
    terminal)
  prune [-dry-run] [-yes]
    delete Completed sessions
  loop <subcommand> [args]
    repeat loops: re-send a prompt until
    a check passes
  log <sel> [flags]
    print a session's transcript (-f
    follows)

Daemon:
  status [flags]
    session counts; exit 1 if one needs
    input
  daemon start|stop|restart|status|logs
    manage the rex-daemon
  reload [flags]
    reload tools.yaml, config,
    config.lua and init.lua in the
    daemon
  upgrade [-cold] [-yes] [flags]
    load a newly installed build: hot-
    restart the daemon, swap every board

Insights:
  errors [-n N] [-since 24h] [-clear]
    failed rex commands from the error
    log
  overview [flags]
    one-screen summary of every session
    by bucket
  export <sel> [flags]
    write a session as a readable
    document
  usage [flags]
    tokens, cost and plan quota per
    agent and model
  audit [flags]
    one line per finished session (needs
    audit_trail)
  digest [flags]
    today's sessions, time and totals
  stats [flags]
    lifetime usage by model and tool
  fleet ls|show|set|unset
    list or edit session fleets

Lifecycle:
  setup [flags]
    guided first-run wizard (-yes for
    defaults)
  onboard [flags]
    guided tour for new users: checks,
    agents, keys
  doctor [flags]
    check the install; exit 1 if a check
    fails
  update [flags]
    upgrade rex in place (-check only
    looks)
  uninstall [flags]
    remove rex and optional state

Other:
  skills [flags]
    list the skills library
    (~/.config/rex/skills)
  config list|get|set|reset|edit
    view and change settings
  theme list|show|new
    list, inspect and create color
    themes
  trust [dir] [-ls] [-rm <dir>]
    trust a project folder so agents
    skip the trust dialog
  ws init|id|ls|rename|color|trust|open
    workspaces: mark a project folder
    (needs workspaces)
  render [flags]
    render an event stream from stdin
  completion bash|zsh|fish
    print a shell completion script
  version
    print the version
  agent-help
    the usage card for LLM agents

Output:
  -o, --output FORMAT
    text | txt | md | json | agent (txt
    when piped)
  --agent
    one line per record, no color, no
    prompts
  --no-color
    never emit ANSI color

Selectors: short id (4+ hex), slug or
full id.

Run "rex <command> -h" for flags ·
agents: rex agent-help
